🪶 **NIT: AC2 pins the latch only as `isNotEmpty` — assert the exact key set**

In the new gh-2270 test group, AC1 and the border test both pin the latch to the exact orphan key:

```dart
expect(latch, {key});
// border test:
expect(latch, {
  orphanReportKey(_orphanContext()[1] as ToolResultMessage),
});
```

but AC2's delivery round only checks membership is non-empty (`test/agent/orphan_notice_loop_test.dart:345`):

```dart
expect(latch, isNotEmpty);
```

The one-shot contract this PR ships is "the latch gains exactly the delivered batch" — a weaker `isNotEmpty` would keep passing if the latch ever picked up stray keys (or if the batch grew). Asserting `expect(latch, {key})` makes all three new tests pin the contract symmetrically and costs nothing (the context is the same single-orphan fixture).
